  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing civil society ability to Monitor Key Aspects of national governance and policy making proc</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 1 year project intend to be rolled out to help bridge the gaps and input into the process of constitution making as well as other key policy making processes in South Sudan, with possibility of extending another year. The project aims at ensuring meaningful citizen participation in the various processes of constitution making and other policies at National and state levels to cultivate the spirit of nationalism among South Sudanese. SuDEMOP therefore being aware of the need for peaceful environment to facilitate smooth participation of citizens in national process, will monitoring key aspects of policy making, governance processes and disseminating timely and accurate information to citizens so as to enhance citizen understanding of issues pertaining policy making both as right owner and duty bearer. This project will enable citizens to make informed decisions on policy and governance issues while engaging with government leaders and other policy makers at grassroots and national level.</narrative>
  </description>
